// (1533; English trans. 1651) — the "Seals or Characters of the Planets".
// One figure per classical planet, drawn behind the generated sigil as a
// faint watermark.
//
// Vectorized (filled-outline trace) from public-domain reproductions of the
// original woodcuts:
//   Saturn, Jupiter, Mars, Sun, Venus, Mercury — scans of the 1533 Cologne
//     edition, Wikimedia Commons (Category: Seals and characters of the planets).
//   Moon — public-domain woodcut reproduction (Twilit Grotto / Esoteric
//     Archives, Of Occult Philosophy, Book II, figure 2-60).
//
// Each string is one SVG path (multiple subpaths, even-odd fill), centred on
// (180, 180) and normalized so every point lies within radius 160 of the
// centre — the figure stays inside the planetary ring once scaled.

